From a5ab4fdb7dcbf3a3ddf59ae9f3024888dd4a7327 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 19:05:28 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 14/60] TP RoCE: a failed transport halts its QPs, drains them
 and keeps its region; the region is DONTFORK and NOHUGEPAGE

A local protection error can arrive while the IOMMU invalidates its mappings lazily. On such an error the old path
left the other HCA's QP ready to send (still taking the peer's writes), hung up the fate channel without telling
the peer to stop, and freed the region at once: unregistered from CUDA with no GPU sync, then QP destroy, MR
deregistration and munmap. A device write after the unmap could then reach a reused page through a stale IOTLB entry.

- Roce.fail and Roce.abort (the fail-fast hook) move every QP to the error state: no send goes out and no peer write
  lands.
- Roce.deinit quiesces first: QPs to error, every posted request reaped (flushed or not), cuCtxSynchronize. A failed
  transport, or one that does not quiesce, keeps its region registered and mapped; the process exit tears it down.
- Session.close on a failed transport goes fail-fast before closing, so the peer aborts and halts its HCAs first.
- The region is MADV_DONTFORK and MADV_NOHUGEPAGE before ibv_reg_mr; a refusal fails the start.
- A QP whose actual max_inline_data is under 4 B is refused (the flag post uses lkey 0 on a stack word).
- One log line a rank: region base and length, each HCA's lkey and rkey, the peer's region and rkeys.

Tests: on fake verbs Roce.abort halts both QPs; quiesce halts both before the first flush and reaps every posted write;
an aborted transport reports itself failed, and over the shm wire the aborted rank keeps its region while the other
frees it; smaps shows dc and nh on a prepared region; the inline bound refuses 3 B and takes 4.

(cherry picked from commit 4ad5029960fb26959b8787833aa04c39a131afaf)
